  parent: gru_v041
  status: planned
description: v041 with hidden 128 -> 192, i.e. our student at the SAME hidden width
  as the teacher it distils from. v041 is the best full-validation score in the project
  at 0.689036; everything else it holds fixed (pair teacher, distill_weight 3.0, 3
  epochs) is the winning recipe.
hypothesis: 'The external probe settled what v039''s config got wrong. Measured on
  500 identical validation sequences, dozken''s reset4k scores 0.709584 against our
  v039''s 0.703872 -- the TEACHER is +0.005712 BETTER than the student on our own
  rows and our own metric. v039''s config had argued the opposite, and the error is
  legible: it compared our subset number against dozken''s number from a DIFFERENT
  192-sequence held-out set, so the two were never on the same scale and the comparison
  could not have held. The teacher is also 2x WIDER -- hidden 192 / 435,943 params
  against our hidden 128 / 225,922. That gives a concrete, testable reason the gap
  stays open: the student is capacity-limited relative to the thing it is distilling
  from, so it cannot represent the teacher''s function however much supervision we
  give it. v041 already pushed distill_weight to 3.0 and gained, consistent with ''more
  signal helps'', but supervision cannot exceed capacity. This is the one axis where
  ''make the student bigger'' has a positive prior rather than the negative one that
  closed the capacity question in v034-v036 -- and the reason is that v034''s hidden
  192 regressed 12.4 sigma with NO teacher to absorb the extra capacity, which is
  a different experiment from this one.'
change_vs_parent: model.hidden 128 -> 192. Single change versus v041.
